    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "547:2789",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Camping Site",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Camping Site"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Weekend in the Countryside\n\nLast summer, my family went camping for the first time. We drove to a campsite in the Lake District, about three hours from our home.\n\nWhen we arrived, the campsite warden showed us to our pitch — a flat area of grass where we could set up our tent. My father and I unpacked the car and started putting up the tent. It took about forty minutes because neither of us had done it before. The instructions were confusing, but eventually we managed to get all the poles in place and hammer the pegs into the ground with a mallet.\n\nThe campsite had basic facilities: a shower block with hot water, a toilet block, a washing-up area for cleaning dishes, and a small shop that sold essentials like bread, milk, and firewood.\n\nIn the evening, we lit a campfire in the fire pit and cooked sausages on a portable barbecue. We also roasted marshmallows on sticks. The sky was incredibly clear, and we could see thousands of stars — something we never see in the city because of light pollution.\n\nThe next morning, I woke up early. The air was cool and fresh, and I could hear birds singing. We had breakfast outside — cereal, toast cooked on a camping stove, and hot chocolate.\n\nAfter breakfast, we went on a hike through the woods and along the lake. We saw rabbits, squirrels, and a heron standing in the shallow water. The walk took about two hours.\n\nWhen it was time to leave on Sunday afternoon, we took down the tent, packed up our gear, and made sure we left no rubbish behind. The campsite rule is 'Leave no trace.'",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "A Weekend in the Countryside Last summer, my family went camping for the first time. We drove to a campsite in the Lake District, about three hours from our home. When we arrived, the campsite warden showed us to our pitch — a flat area of grass where we could set up our tent. My father and I unpacked the car and started putting up the tent. It took about forty minutes because neither of us had done it before. The instructions were confusing, but eventually we managed to get all the poles in place and hammer the pegs into the ground with a mallet. The campsite had basic facilities: a shower block with hot water, a toilet block, a washing-up area for cleaning dishes, and a small shop that sold essentials like bread, milk, and firewood. In the evening, we lit a campfire in the fire pit and cooked sausages on a portable barbecue. We also roasted marshmallows on sticks. The sky was incredibly clear, and we could see thousands of stars — something we never see in the city because of light pollution. The next morning, I woke up early. The air was cool and fresh, and I could hear birds singing. We had breakfast outside — cereal, toast cooked on a camping stove, and hot chocolate. After breakfast, we went on a hike through the woods and along the lake. We saw rabbits, squirrels, and a heron standing in the shallow water. The walk took about two hours. When it was time to leave on Sunday afternoon, we took down the tent, packed up our gear, and made sure we left no rubbish behind. The campsite rule is 'Leave no trace.'"
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. Where did the family go camping?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. Where did the family go camping?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. Why did setting up the tent take so long?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. Why did setting up the tent take so long?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What facilities did the campsite have?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What facilities did the campsite have?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. Why could they see more stars at the campsite than at home?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. Why could they see more stars at the campsite than at home?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What does 'Leave no trace' mean?",
          "depth": 1,
